    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PSA\nN7IPS\nElectra\nJET\nPSA",
      "PSA- - PACIFIC SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\nLockheed L-188C Electra\nPSA, then an intra-state airline operating wholly. with-\nin the State of California,\nreceived its first Electra\n(shown on this card) in November 1959. In a few\nyears, PSA became the dominant air carrier in the\nState, much of its success being attributed to the\npopularity and reliability\nof_ the Electra. In 1968\nthe airline sold its\nentire\nElectra fleet,\nreplacing\nthem with 727's.\nThis particular Electra was re-\npurchased in 1975 for use on a newly awarded\nroute\nwhich was unsuitable for currently available\npure jet aircraft.\nPhoto courtesy Lockheed-California Company\nPub. by Aviation World, Inc., P.O. Box 188, Bethel, Conn. 06801, U.S.A.\nN171PS c/n 1091\nL-009/61036-D\npost card\n2015.166.1195"
